---
title: Voice Room — Live Voice Chat · danbot lab
description: "A free browser voice chat room for up to 6 people. Walk around a shared house — living room, game room, TV room, private room — and talk with proximity and line-of-sight voice, peer-to-peer over WebRTC. No download, no sign-up."
extraCss:
  - /games/voice/voice.css
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block content %}
<div id="canvas-wrap" class="canvas-wrap">
    <canvas id="house-canvas"></canvas>
</div>

<button id="btn-menu" class="menu-btn" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="side-menu" title="Menu">
    <span class="menu-btn-icon">☰</span>
</button>

<div id="menu-backdrop" class="menu-backdrop hidden"></div>

<aside id="side-menu" class="side-menu" aria-label="Voice room menu">
    <div class="side-menu__inner">
        <a href="/" class="menu-home-link">← danbot lab</a>
        <h1 class="menu-title">Voice Room</h1>
        <p id="status-banner" class="status-banner">Connecting…</p>

        <div id="self-bar" class="self-bar hidden">
            <button id="btn-mute" class="act-btn" aria-pressed="false">Mute</button>
            <div class="self-meta">
                <span id="self-name" class="self-name"></span>
                <div id="self-level-track" class="level-track" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div id="self-level-bar" class="level-bar"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <button id="btn-leave" class="act-btn fold">Leave</button>
        </div>

        <section class="settings-section">
            <h3>Your name</h3>
            <input type="text" id="settings-name" maxlength="16" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Your name…">
        </section>

        <section class="settings-section">
            <h3>Your color</h3>
            <div id="settings-color-row" class="color-row"></div>
        </section>

        <section class="settings-section">
            <h3>Player token</h3>
            <p class="settings-hint">Your name and color are saved under this token. Copy it to restore your
                identity on another device, or paste one here to load a saved profile.</p>
            <div class="token-row">
                <input type="text" id="settings-token" readonly>
                <button id="settings-token-copy" class="act-btn small" type="button">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <div class="token-row">
                <input type="text" id="settings-token-input" placeholder="Paste a token to load…" autocomplete="off">
                <button id="settings-token-load" class="act-btn small" type="button">Load</button>
            </div>
            <p id="settings-token-msg" class="settings-msg"></p>
        </section>

        <section class="settings-section">
            <h3>Volume per person</h3>
            <div id="peer-volume-list" class="peer-volume-list"></div>
        </section>

        <p id="room-hint" class="room-hint">
            Click or tap the floor to walk. Volume follows distance and line of sight — full
            volume up close, a faint murmur through walls, silence across the house.
        </p>

        <details id="how-it-works">
            <summary>How it works &amp; privacy</summary>
            <p>Audio travels <strong>directly between browsers</strong> (peer-to-peer
            WebRTC). The server only introduces players to each other and relays everyone's
            position in the house; your voice never passes through it. Because connections are
            direct, peers can see each other's IP addresses — fine among friends, worth knowing
            in general.</p>
            <p>Volume is <strong>proximity and line-of-sight based</strong>: walk close to
            someone with a clear line of sight for full volume, hear a muffled murmur from
            adjacent rooms through the wall, and lose someone entirely once they're far enough
            away. Each person also has a <strong>volume slider</strong> above that boosts or cuts
            them on top of that.</p>
            <p>Some restrictive or corporate networks block direct connections. If someone can't
            be heard, a relay (TURN) server would be needed — not yet configured for this casual
            room.</p>
        </details>
    </div>
</aside>

<!-- Name prompt -->
<div id="name-overlay" class="overlay">
    <div class="overlay-card">
        <h2>Join the voice room</h2>
        <p>Pick a name and color, then allow microphone access.</p>
        <input type="text" id="name-input" placeholder="Your name…" maxlength="16" autocomplete="off">
        <div id="join-color-row" class="color-row centered"></div>
        <div id="name-error" class="name-error hidden"></div>
        <div class="name-actions">
            <button id="name-submit" class="act-btn raise">Join &amp; enable mic</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
<script type="module" src="/games/voice/voice.js"></script>
{% endblock %}
